---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
warning[lossy_xx]: `xx` converts `s64` to `u16`, which can lose the high bits
  --> tests/lint/lossy_xx/bad.jai:5:18
   |
 5 |     small: u16 = xx big;
   |                  ^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(u16)` to make the conversion visible
   |
 4       big := 70000;
 5 ~     small: u16 = cast(u16) big;
 6       ratio := 2.75;
   |
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/lossy_xx

warning[lossy_xx]: `xx` converts `float32` to `s64`, which drops the fraction
  --> tests/lint/lossy_xx/bad.jai:7:18
   |
 7 |     whole: int = xx ratio;
   |                  ^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(s64)` to make the conversion visible
   |
 6       ratio := 2.75;
 7 ~     whole: int = cast(s64) ratio;
 8       precise: float64 = 1.0 / 3.0;
   |
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/lossy_xx

warning[lossy_xx]: `xx` converts `float64` to `float32`, which can lose precision
  --> tests/lint/lossy_xx/bad.jai:9:22
   |
 9 |     rough: float32 = xx precise;
   |                      ^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(float32)` to make the conversion visible
   |
 8       precise: float64 = 1.0 / 3.0;
 9 ~     rough: float32 = cast(float32) precise;
10
   |
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/lossy_xx
